{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For they abased themselves</b> — For behold you teach, just as the wicked were abased, you would say גֹּהָה [exalt yourself] like גֵּאָה. And the meaning: for pride abased them, as in the matter of 'before destruction, pride.'" "<b>And He saves the lowly of eyes</b> — The reference is: 'also He will deliver the innocent island.' Some say that it is deficient of a shin and its meaning is 'innocent man,' but this is far-fetched. Therefore its meaning: that the Place [God] saves the lowly of eyes, who is a single man. 'Also He will deliver the innocent island,' like 'the inhabitant of this island,' and its opposite: 'when a land sins against Me.'" "<b>And delivered by the cleanness of your hands</b> — And you shall be delivered by the cleanness of your hands."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:37.956990679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}